OL,3,GNEWSACouncil leader says cliff
OL,4,Asculpture 'not my cup of tea'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA new #54,000 art sculpture installed
OL,7,Fin a Bournemouth clifftop has been
OL,8,Fdescribed as "not my cup of tea" by the
OL,9,Fleader of the local council.
OL,11,FThe Lean Into the Wind installation is
OL,12,Fpart of a government-funded Coastal
OL,13,FPublic Art and Heritage Trail and was
OL,14,Funveiled on Bournemouth's West Cliff
OL,15,Flast month.
OL,17,FAt a Bournemouth, Christchurch and
OL,18,FPoole (BCP) Council meeting a
OL,19,Fcouncillor asked whether the authority
OL,20,Fwas also seeking funding for frontline
OL,21,Fservices.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,334,330,200,160,0,100
